   "id": "SQ-VALUE",
   "assumption": "start == 1 && in >= 4 && in <= 8 ##1 (quiet x11)",
   "guarantee": "out == 2",
   "why_not_minable": "the design drives its own input port back to zero after latching, so the operand is invisible when the result appears. Pinning the result therefore needs both an operand range in the assumption AND a quiet-window sequence to fix the sampling cycle, and neither the range-plus-sequence antecedent nor the exact-latency form is in any template. This is the concrete case for the paper's 'mined guarantee weaker than the reference' classification",
   "minable": false
  },
